WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.402 size:84% position:42%
-When you tell people
you have five children,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's probably
a bit of a gasp.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:07.073
-Oh, there is -- It's a gasp,
but my wife is one of nine,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.109 line:92%
and so she comes from this

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:12.178 size:78% position:39%
insanely large family
that's very close.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.580 line:92%
They do everything together.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.717
Like, over Christmas, I went
to a movie with 30 people.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not even making that --
We were walking around.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
People thought
we were from a church.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:25.525 line:92%
To put it in perspective,

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jesus only walked around
with 12.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I learned very quickly,
being married,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.801
that I don't want to do anything
with 30 people.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.102 line:92%
Like, if I was on the "Titanic"

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.471 size:88% position:44%
and the last rescue boat
was full with 30 people,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like,
"You guys go ahead.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.142 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I don't want to be there

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.878 size:84% position:42%
when you try and decide
where to eat lunch."

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they're amazing.
-Are you close?

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you become close
with her extended family?

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
they're amazing people.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:55.789 size:78% position:39%
And my wife's parents
are special people.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
Their names
are Louise and Dominic.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.225 line:92%
I call them Louise and Dom.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.362
But my wife's siblings
have also gotten married,

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
and some of their spouses
call Louise and Dom

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mom" and "Dad,"
because they're weirdos.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.537 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know, it's like --

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, do you call your in-laws
Mom and Dad?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-'Cause it's like --

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
I understand sometimes
people marry into a family,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.812
and you become so close
to their spouse's parents

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they want to call them
Mom and Dad, but don't!

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's weird and confusing
for the rest of us.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"Wait. That's his mom?

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.790 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He married his sister?"

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"What state is he from?"

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.766 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a new tour --
Quality Time Tour.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Quality Time Tour.
-That's very exciting.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
You like being on the road?
-I love it. I love it.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.873 line:92%
It's just amazing going around.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to Canada this week.
So it's a good time.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.912
Well, there is --
Nobody's better at it than you.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.582
That's why I've always liked you
more than Mulaney.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.185
-John Mulaney.
He likes me more than you, John!

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up for
Jim Gaffigan, everybody!

